<title>UK: British utilities outline windfall tax liability.</title>
<headline>British utilities outline windfall tax liability.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reuters is compiling a list of company estimates for possible levies under a one-off tax on excess profits of privatised utilities announced by Chancellor Gordon Brown in his first budget on July 2.</p>
<p>Brown said the tax should raise around 2.1 billion stg from the electricity sector, around 1.65 billion from water companies and 1.45 billion from others, giving a total 5.2 billion.</p>
<p>The tax will be charged at a rate of 23 percent on the difference between company value at the time of flotation and company value calculated by reference to profits over a period up to four years following privatisation.</p>
<p>The following table lists companies and their estimates for payments under the so-called &quot;windfall&quot; tax.</p>
<p>Figures are in million stg.</p>
<p>Electricity (to raise 2.1 billion stg) --</p>
<p>Electricity generators --</p>
<p>National Power Plc 261</p>
<p>PowerGen Plc 200</p>
<p>Scottish Hydro-Electric Plc 45</p>
<p>Scottish Power Plc -- no company figures available</p>
<p>(which also owns which owns Southern Water and</p>
<p>Manweb)</p>
<p>British Energy Plc nil</p>
<p>The regional electricity companies(RECs), owners follow in brackets --</p>
<p>London Electricity (Entergy Corp )140</p>
<p>Northern Electric (CE Electric )118</p>
<p>East Midlands (Dominion Resources )n/a</p>
<p>South Western (Southern Co )	 97</p>
<p>Seeboard (Central &amp; South West )110</p>
<p>Midlands Electricity (Avon Energy, a joint</p>
<p>venture between GPU Inc and CINergy</p>
<p>)130</p>
<p>Hyder Plc, which owns Welsh Water</p>
<p>and South Wales Electricity 280</p>
<p>United Utilities Plc, which owns North</p>
<p>West Water and Norweb -- no company figures available</p>
<p>Eastern Electric (Energy Group Plc )112</p>
<p>Yorkshire Electricity (American Electric Power</p>
<p>and Public Service Co of Colorado )135</p>
<p>Southern Electric Plc 165</p>
<p>Northern Ireland Electricity Plc  44</p>
<p>The water and sewerage companies (to raise 1.65 billion) --</p>
<p>Northumbrian Water</p>
<p>(Lyonnaise des Eaux SA ) 79</p>
<p>Anglian Water Plc 170</p>
<p>Thames Water Plc 230</p>
<p>Wessex Water Plc 99</p>
<p>Severn Trent Plc -- no company figures available</p>
<p>South West Water Plc 100</p>
<p>Yorkshire Water Plc n/a</p>
<p>Others (to raise around 1.45 billion) --</p>
<p>Airport operator BAA Plc 70-100</p>
<p>The former British Gas companies --</p>
<p>BG Plc 513</p>
<p>Centrica Plc 190</p>
<p>British Telecommunications Plc 500</p>
<p>Railtrack Plc up to 160</p>
